WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.968
Let's start with the

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:05.405
attack on Pelosi's husband, Paul Pelosi.

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.707
What is your reaction

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.043
It's disgusting.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.379
This this this violence is horrible.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:14.414
You know, that's happened.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.716
We had a door knocker in Florida

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.550
that was attacked.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.853
I mean, this stuff is has to stop.

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.022
One thing I did when I took over the NRC

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:22.889
a year

00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:24.057
and a half ago is

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.158
I went to the Federal Election

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:25.759
Commission, said

00:00:25.759 --> 00:00:28.194
could our candidates and our senators

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.529
use their campaign dollars

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:30.964
to pay for security?

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.532
Because as you know,

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.433
how sensitive members

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.300
don't have security,

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.136
most of them outside of D.C.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:37.937
So but a lot of it is we got to

00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:39.839
we've got to say, let's let's have a

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.241
we can have a heated conversation

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:42.208
about the issues,

00:00:42.208 --> 00:00:44.110
but this violence has got to stop.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.378
This is this is horrible.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:47.514
And my heart goes out to Paul Pelosi.

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:49.182
And I hope he has a full recovery.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.683
We've learned that the suspect's

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.585
social media

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:53.620
shows that he embraced

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:54.721
conspiracy theories

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.989
about the 2020 election.

00:00:55.989 --> 00:00:57.090
And January six,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:57.924
I want you to listen to what

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.559
President Biden said yesterday.

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.798
It's one thing to condemn the violence,

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:06.800
but you can't condemn the violence

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:08.635
unless you condemn those people

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.370
continue to argue

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.505
the election was not real

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:14.507
that is being stolen

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:16.743
that all the all the Milwaukee

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:18.211
that's been put out there

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.547
to undermine democracy.

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.081
Is he right?

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:22.015
Should Republicans

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:22.982
do more to reject

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.217
conspiracy theories

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.619
and dangerous rhetoric

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:29.322
I think what we have to do is, one,

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.157
we have to condemn the violence

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.358
and that we have to do everything

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:32.792
we can

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.094
to get people to make sure

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:34.861
people feel comfortable

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.296
about these elections.

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:36.996
You know, we've got to

00:01:36.996 --> 00:01:37.831
we've got to do everything

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:38.498
we can to get

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:39.566
people comfortable

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.768
that this election in nine days

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.503
is going to be free and fair,

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.604
that people's votes are

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.206
all going to be counted fairly.

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:47.540
They're not going to be diluted.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.475
And so that's one thing

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.109
I've tried to do at

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:51.511
the NRC is get people to make sure

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:52.879
we're ready.

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:53.446
I tell people,

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:53.813
go to the

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.181
go to the polls, vote,

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:57.450
go to the polls, and be poll watchers.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.119
So you can see that these elections

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.320
are going to be free and fair.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.287
And we've got to work on it

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.489
every every cycle,

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:05.158
get it better every every, every cycle.

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.459
To be fair, Senator,

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:09.429
most of your Republican colleagues,

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.297
even those in the Trump White House,

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:12.866
said that the 20, 20 election

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:13.900
was free and fair.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.001
And that has not stopped

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.603
the conspiracies from flying.

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:19.405
So is it important for people

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:20.707
from the top of your party,

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.442
the former president, on down

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.409
to tone down

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:23.910
the rhetoric

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.011
about the conspiracies

00:02:25.011 --> 00:02:26.412
that might instigate it,

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.648
somebody who is unhinged, like

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:32.218
the man who went into the Pelosi home

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:35.822
Then I think what's

00:02:35.822 --> 00:02:36.956
important is everybody

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:37.624
do everything we can

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.993
to make these elections fair.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.094
We've got Hillary Clinton

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:43.229
saying the 24 elections could be stolen.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.598
We've got Stacey Abrams saying she didn't

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.133
she didn't lose.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:47.267
Know.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.535
So my job is

00:02:48.535 --> 00:02:50.403
do everything I can to get people

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:51.204
to feel comfortable.

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:52.639
These elections are fair.

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:54.707
And I'm telling people get out to vote.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:56.242
Colby, a poll watcher.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.710
And when we have the opportunity,

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:59.145
let's make our election laws safer.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.548
Let's make sure that you have voter I.D.,

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:03.249
you don't have ballot harvesting

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.617
you have monitor ballot box

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.052
that makes people feel more comfortable

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:07.754
that the elections are going to be fair.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:08.588
And just to be clear,

00:03:08.588 --> 00:03:09.255
I want to move on,

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.057
but there is no evidence

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.326
that they weren't fair in 2020.

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.295
I do want to move on to something

00:03:15.295 --> 00:03:16.095
that's happening

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.430
happened in your home

00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.731
state of Florida

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:19.566
which is

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:20.466
reporting that there were

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.135
anti-Semitic displays around

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:23.403
yesterday's Florida Georgia

00:03:23.403 --> 00:03:25.171
football game in Jacksonville.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.839
Their photos on social media

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:27.941
of people holding

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.176
anti-Semitic signs along the highway.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:33.546
The message Kanye is right about

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.147
the Jews

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.481
was apparently projected

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.683
on the side of the stadium.

00:03:36.683 --> 00:03:37.550
What's your reaction

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:40.653
machine mad?

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:41.221
You know I

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.289
became governor in January in 2011

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.490
and we were dealing with this

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.059
at one of our universities.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.093
We've dealt with it.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.395
I've had I've dealt with it as governor

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.232
and this anti-Semitism.

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.601
What I mean, it's it's disgusting.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.002
It's wrong.

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.738
We have to push back against that.

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.873
And I mean, we've got to understand, we

00:04:01.341 --> 00:04:02.342
we are blessed.

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:03.243
We live in a country

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.178
where we need to accept people.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.412
We need to do

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:08.348
we can cherish our differences.

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:10.016
But let's let's accept people

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.251
and let's all live in a country

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.585
that we gets

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:13.653
we've got the best opportunity

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.721
in the world.

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:16.623
So let's quit dividing ourselves

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.558
and quit attacking other people.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:19.359
And just talk about

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.893
how we make this a better place.

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.463
So this stuff is disgusting to me.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:24.664
I've never understood

00:04:24.664 --> 00:04:26.866
it, and it's disgusting to me.

00:04:26.866 --> 00:04:28.434
Well, let's talk about your midterms.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:29.102
Agenda.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:31.070
Democrats say that

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.105
one of your proposals

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.773
that which would sunset

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:35.074
all federal legislation

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.943
after five years jeopardizes

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.611
Medicare and Social Security.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.812
You've previously said that

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:40.546
those programs

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.181
need to be preserved,

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:43.783
reformed and protected.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.652
So just a simple yes or no.

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:46.419
Do Republicans

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:48.388
want to cut Medicare

00:04:48.388 --> 00:04:49.856
and or Social Security

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:52.892
Absolutely not.

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:53.893
And, you know, the Democrats

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.862
just cut $280 billion.

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.597
All Democrats in the Senate and House

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:59.565
voted to cut $280 billion

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:02.468
out of Medicare just to two months ago.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:03.836
And then they want to say

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.705
Republicans want to cut something.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:07.373
Democrats have done this.

00:05:07.373 --> 00:05:08.508
So when he was sent

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:09.976
or said he wanted to cut Medicare

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:10.943
and Social Security,

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:12.578
I believe we got to preserve them

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:15.181
and make sure we we we keep them.

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:16.382
What I want to do

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.418
is make sure we live within our means

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.553
and make sure we preserve those programs.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:21.487
People paid into them.

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:22.455
They believe in them.

00:05:22.455 --> 00:05:23.222
I believe them.

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.524
I'm going to fight like hell

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:25.692
to make sure we preserve

00:05:25.692 --> 00:05:26.993
Medicare and Social Security.

00:05:26.993 --> 00:05:28.561
Just want to correct the record.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:30.496
The Democrats plan, which is now law,

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:30.797
it didn't

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.231
cut social

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:32.799
excuse me,

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:34.600
it didn't cut Medicare benefits.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.969
It allowed for negotiation

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.638
for prescription drug prices,

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:39.038
which would

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:40.807
ultimately bring down the price

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:43.109
and the cost for Medicare consumers.

00:05:43.142 --> 00:05:44.477
But I want to ask the next question,

00:05:44.477 --> 00:05:46.079
which is about raising.

00:05:46.079 --> 00:05:47.447
Could we just finish that, though?

00:05:47.447 --> 00:05:48.481
Is it cut to

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:50.717
and then it cut to an $80 billion

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:51.551
out of Medicare?

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:52.885
That means we're going to have fewer

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:53.853
life saving drugs.

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:56.556
It cut $280 billion in Medicare.

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:57.790
They can say they would

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.326
cut $80 billion

00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:02.995
had benefits or reduce life saving drugs.

00:06:04.263 --> 00:06:04.831
It didn't.

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:05.498
You can do that,

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:06.032
but you don't have

00:06:06.032 --> 00:06:07.400
to make sure something's going to happen.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:07.867
All right.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:08.501
Come on.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:08.735
All right.

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:11.104
I mean, I want to we can debate that

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:12.939
for a long time,

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:13.873
but I want to focus on

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.341
you and the Republicans

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:16.676
and what you want to do right now.

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:17.777
Do you support raising

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:20.246
the eligibility age for Medicare?

00:06:20.246 --> 00:06:22.081
And Social Security?

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:24.183
No.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:24.951
Okay.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:25.685
Do you support

00:06:25.685 --> 00:06:27.620
cutting back on Medicare benefits

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.123
or reducing Social Security payments

00:06:30.123 --> 00:06:32.291
in order to keep the program solvent?

00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:35.061
No, I don't.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:37.630
No one Republican that does

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.098
and I know Joe Biden proposed

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:41.501
you know, he believed in these things.

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:43.002
He said it publicly when he was a U.S.

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:43.436
senator.

00:06:44.971 --> 00:06:46.339
Let's talk about

00:06:46.339 --> 00:06:47.740
another part of your plan

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.275
which calls for permanently

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:51.944
extending the 2017 Trump tax cuts.

00:06:52.278 --> 00:06:53.646
Many economists say

00:06:53.646 --> 00:06:55.681
that could make inflation worse.

00:06:55.982 --> 00:06:56.883
The nonpartisan

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:58.050
Congressional Budget Office

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.818
says it would add

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:01.621
almost $3 trillion to the deficit.

00:07:01.888 --> 00:07:03.890
So how is that fiscally responsible

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:08.661
Well, here's my experience.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:09.796
I cut taxes and fees

00:07:09.796 --> 00:07:11.964
100 times as governor of Florida,

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.267
and my revenues grew.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:16.602
Revenues grew with the Trump tax cuts.

00:07:16.602 --> 00:07:17.370
They didn't go down.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.405
They grew with the Trump tax cuts.

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:20.573
Inflation is caused

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.775
by not living within our means,

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:24.210
by having a government

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.111
that spends more than

00:07:25.111 --> 00:07:26.612
it takes in buy,

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:28.981
because in a regulatory environment

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:29.882
that makes it difficult

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:31.751
for people to produce foods.

00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:33.085
Having a regulatory environment

00:07:33.085 --> 00:07:34.387
that causes gas prices to go

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:35.421
up, have diesel prices

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:37.590
to go up, and natural gas prices go up.

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:39.926
That's what causes inflation.

00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:40.993
Inflation is not caused

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:43.529
because you cut taxes. Government is not.

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:45.565
Government does not create the economy.

00:07:45.565 --> 00:07:47.733
Individuals create the economy.

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:48.901
Businesses create the

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.269
economy, not government.

00:07:51.437 --> 00:07:52.104
Well.

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:53.873
Okay. Well,

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:56.209
on the question of inflation,

00:07:56.209 --> 00:07:58.277
the Congressional Budget Office

00:07:58.277 --> 00:08:00.613
is the one that said that

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:01.614
reviving the Trump

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:03.783
tax cuts, extending them permanently.

00:08:03.783 --> 00:08:04.484
I should say

00:08:04.484 --> 00:08:05.017
would add

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:07.253
almost $3 trillion to the deficit.

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:09.489
You think they're wrong?

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:09.956
That's.

00:08:09.956 --> 00:08:10.623
That's assuming

00:08:10.623 --> 00:08:11.991
you don't grow the economy.

00:08:11.991 --> 00:08:12.458
I mean,

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:13.259
I cut taxes

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:16.162
100 times and fees at times as government

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.331
revenues grew

00:08:18.331 --> 00:08:19.398
because you start building

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:20.299
the private sector.

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:21.868
We got to make government smaller,

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:23.336
the private sector bigger.

00:08:23.336 --> 00:08:24.670
That's what we have to do.

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:26.372
This idea that government can build

00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:28.741
an economy is just a complete fallacy.

00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:30.109
And it's never worked anywhere.

00:08:30.109 --> 00:08:30.576
It does it.

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:31.210
It's not worked.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.478
As we get bigger and bigger government,

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:34.180
we get more and more inflation.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.882
I mean, it's very consistent.

00:08:35.882 --> 00:08:37.884
The election is just nine days away.

